config NOTHING_WRITRBACK_KMSG
	tristate "Nothing boot/panic kmsg writeback to logdump"
	default n
	help
	  Writes a rolling copy of the kernel log to the logdump partition
	  throughout boot (ported from Nothing's stock 5.4 nothing_stability
	  driver). Doesn't log any customer info. When the device is stuck,
	  this can help debug it: the partition can be read back with
	  dd on a later, working boot (adb root required), independent of
	  USB/display state during the stuck boot itself.
